 "as_of": "2026-10-01",
 "summary": "Unit covers the eastern and southern communes of Kinshasa (Matete, Lemba, Kisenso, Selembao, Binza Meteo/Ozone, Mont Ngafula, Masina II, Kingasani, Biyela, Nsele) and the rural commune of Maluku. The capital is firmly state-held: day-to-day order in the urban neighbourhoods is kept by the Police Nationale Congolaise (district commissariats, PIR/LENI units), with FARDC and Republican Guard garrisons in the city; kuluna youth gangs commit frequent robberies and assaults, especially in peripheral hillside neighbourhoods (Kisenso, Selembao, Mont Ngafula), but do not displace police authority and are targeted by recurrent police operations. Peri-urban localities of Nsele, Mont Ngafula, Biyela and western Maluku (Maluku centre, Kinkole-Kimpoko axis, DAIPN camps, Kibomango) are state/PNC areas with notable FARDC presence (Kibomango training centre, DAIPN). The eastern Batéké plateau part of Maluku bordering Kwamouth (Mai-Ndombe) has seen Mobondo militia incursions since 2023-2024, answered by FARDC deployments; it is assessed as an FARDC-held operation zone with Mobondo raiding, at low confidence. NOTE: web research was unavailable for this unit (search budget exhausted, egress blocked), so the assessment rests on prior background knowledge only.",
